# Frontmatter Contract

> **Machine-readable schema:** `tooling/schemas/frontmatter.schema.json` (JSON Schema draft-07) is the canonical structural definition for all frontmatter fields. This rule is its human-readable companion. When the two disagree, the schema takes precedence for structural constraints; this rule takes precedence for intent and prose guidance.

This rule is the single source of truth for markdown frontmatter fields.

## Required fields for all docs pages

All docs pages under `docs/**/*.md` must include YAML frontmatter with:

```yaml
doc_type: component | overview | foundation | workflow
doc_status: draft | ready | needs-review
```

> **Scope:** `doc_status` applies only to **markdown documentation pages** (`docs/**/*.md`).
> It is distinct from the `status` field in component spec YAML files (`docs/_spec/components/*.yml`),
> which only accepts `draft` or `ready`. The `needs-review` value is not valid in spec YAML files.

## Component page contract (`docs/components/*.md`, excluding `overview.md`)

Component pages must include a `figma` block:

```yaml
figma:
  file_url: "<url-or-TBD>"
  page: "<name-or-TBD>"
  component: "<name-or-TBD>"
  last_verified: "YYYY-MM-DD or TBD"
  # Optional fields (include only when known):
  # component_set_node_id: "123:456"
  # component_hash: "<64-char-sha256>"
  # properties_count: 0
  # variants_count: 0
```

Rules:

- For required string fields, use `TBD` when unknown (never invent values).
- Optional typed fields (`component_set_node_id`, `component_hash`, `properties_count`, `variants_count`) must be omitted when unknown (`TBD` is not valid for these fields).
- `doc_status: ready` requires concrete `figma.last_verified` (not `TBD`).
- If both spec YAML and markdown declare `component_set_node_id`, they must match.
- `component_hash` must be a 64-character SHA-256 hex string when declared.
- `properties_count` and `variants_count` must be non-negative integers when declared.

## Pipeline-generated traceability block

Generated component markdown should include:

```yaml
pipeline:
  ds_component_doc:
    contract_version: "1"
    spec_sha256: "<hash>"
    token_registry_sha256: "<hash>"
    generator_script_sha256: "<hash>"
    content_sha256: "<hash>"
```

Rules:

- All fields are generated by scripts and should not be hand-edited.
- `spec_sha256`: SHA-256 of the component spec YAML at generation time.
- `token_registry_sha256`: SHA-256 of the token registry at generation time.
- `generator_script_sha256`: SHA-256 of the generator script (ds-component-doc.mjs) at generation time.
- `content_sha256`: SHA-256 of the markdown **body** (excluding frontmatter) after generation. Used for drift detection: if the body has changed manually, `content_sha256` will no longer match. Check with `npm run ds:compute-traceability -- --file <path>`.

This block is generated by scripts and should not be hand-edited.

## Schema reference

Full structural constraints — patterns, enums, required fields, and conditional rules — are defined in `tooling/schemas/frontmatter.schema.json`. Key `$defs`:

| Def | Purpose |
| --- | ------- |
| `doc_status` | Enum: `draft \| ready \| needs-review` |
| `figma_node_id` | Pattern `^\d+:\d+$` (sourced from `property-type-map.json`) |
| `sha256_hex` | Pattern `^[0-9a-f]{64}$` (lowercase SHA-256) |
| `date_or_tbd` | ISO 8601 date or the literal `TBD` |
| `url_or_tbd` | Absolute `https?://` URL or the literal `TBD` |
| `pipeline_block` | `pipeline.ds_component_doc` with `contract_version: "1"` |
| `figma_component_block` | Full `figma:` block constraints for component pages |
| `component_page` | Discriminated sub-schema for `doc_type: component` |
| `overview_page` | Discriminated sub-schema for `doc_type: overview` |
| `foundation_page` | Discriminated sub-schema for `doc_type: foundation` |
| `workflow_page` | Discriminated sub-schema for `doc_type: workflow` |
